(559, 43, 'sick', '2026-01-07', '2026-01-09', 'Kindly see attached approved leave last October.  Since we both overlooked the accrual, I am requesting to use my SL instead. I forgot the new process, but as someone who implemented it you should be responsible of giving us the correct data.\n\n As January 5th is my day off, I am only filing 6th-9th. I just got back so I can\'t file the 6th , not sure why is that. Kindly let me know the best step to fix this issue. thanks!', 'rejected', '2026-01-12 04:51:09', NULL, 'lr_69647dbdc7a7a.png', 1, 'Hi Ms. Lovelaine,\r\n\r\nI hope you are doing well.\r\n\r\nRegarding the use of your sick leave credits for your vacation leave, our previous discussion indicated that approval from your Team Lead would be required. However, upon further review, since the requested dates cover a total of three (3) days, a medical certificate will also be necessary.\r\n\r\nThis requirement is in place to ensure compliance in the event that records are reviewed or audited. Consecutive sick leave entries may indicate that an employee was unfit to work during that period. In such cases, we are required to provide medical documentation confirming when the employee was deemed fit to return to work.\r\n\r\nIf you have any questions or need further clarification on this matter kindly email Ms. Cristina Pangan.\r\n\r\nThank you.\r\n\r\nBest regards,'),
